                <pb facs="0753" n="673" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg673"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terres to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-11-05"><hi rendition="#italic">November 5,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Terres reports that Gonaives political refugees are claimed by General Nord;
                    that consul has been instructed not to deliver them, and that Livingston has
                    been instructed to advise the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Cincinnati.</hi>)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
